2026-06-03 16:47:49,087 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As a Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that our company is well-equipped to handle GDPR compliance. We have a Data Protection Officer appointed, and their contact information is dpo@nexus-engineering.it. Our standard data residency policy is EU only, which aligns with the requirement of hosting data exclusively in the EU. 

We also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis. To protect sensitive data, we utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. Additionally, we have implemented various security controls to ensure the protection of personal data.

In terms of access control, we enforce multi-factor authentication using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and we design Role-Based Access Control systems. We also utilize Privileged Access Management solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

Our network security architecture follows patterns such as Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth. We have Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems deployed and experience with DDoS mitigation. Regular penetration testing is conducted annually, and after major releases, with our last test showing 2 medium findings, which were all remediated.

For AI security controls, we protect against prompt injection, redact PII from outputs, detect adversarial inputs, and have a confidence threshold escalation process in place. Model isolation is ensured through an inference API, preventing direct model access for end-users, and security reviews are conducted during model updates.

Our audit and logging practices include logging all queries, using append-only logs with SHA-256 hash chaining for immutability, retaining audit logs for 7 years, and integrating with SIEM tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM in real-time.

To address the specific requirements of not transferring data outside the EU and protecting sensitive data through encryption or anonymization, we can implement data encryption at rest and in transit, ensure that all data processing activities are carried out within the EU, and use our anonymisation tools to protect personal data. 

By leveraging these existing security controls and measures, we can help ensure compliance with GDPR regulations and provide robust protection for personal data.
